# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must NEVER be published (E13-4). `coach dev release-check` applies these rules to decide which files are scanned for
# personal data, so a path ignored here is a path nobody will review: keep this file and docs/release.md consistent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# personal data: keep only the structure/templates of memory/ (the packaged skeleton lives in src/coach/templates/memory/)
memory/*
!memory/README.md
!memory/liabilities/
memory/liabilities/*
!memory/liabilities/_template.yaml
!memory/contracts/
memory/contracts/*
!memory/contracts/_template.yaml
**/data/
.env
*.pem

# local configuration (config.example.toml is the committed template; `coach init` copies it)
config.toml
# your editable copies of the packaged taxonomy / rules (config/import_profiles/ holds shipped examples and IS committed)
config/taxonomy.yaml
config/rules.yaml
# your agent permission file: it holds absolute paths of your machine. The shareable template is docs/claude-settings.example.json
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# E11-2: secrets and web-app state must never be committed, wherever a stray copy ends up
*.key
ui-*.json
.env.*
!.env.example
coach-export-*
*.zip.enc
setup-state.json
# E13-4: the LOCAL list of terms that identify your household (coach dev hygiene --build-terms): never publish it
hygiene-terms*

# docker: the compose volumes and the secrets folder (docs/docker.md)
/coach-home/
/secrets/
docker-compose.override.yml

# database copies and backups
*.plaintext.bak
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.encrypting
*.importing
backups/
*.tar.enc
*.enc

# python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
*.bak
dist/
build/

# web app: dependencies and the production build. The build is NOT committed: CI, the Dockerfile and the release procedure
# (docs/release.md) run `pnpm build`, and the wheel includes it (pyproject: artifacts). In a checkout: `cd web && pnpm install && pnpm build`.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
src/coach/api/static/

# tools
.DS_Store
graphify-out/
